cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DimmerKV, please cite it as below."
title: "DimmerKV: Per-Token Precision for KV Cache Compression in LLM Inference"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Srikanth
    family-names: Balaaji
  - given-names: Sushanth
    family-names: B
  - given-names: T S Sathya
    family-names: Kiran
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SrikanthBalaaji/Dimmer-KV"
url: "https://srikanthbalaaji.github.io/Dimmer-KV/"
abstract: >-
  DimmerKV compresses the KV cache of large language models to 2-5% of its
  FP16 size by giving every token its own precision on top of kvtc-style
  transform coding, refining the tokens a new question needs, and running
  attention directly over the compressed cache. Unlike eviction (H2O,
  SnapKV), it keeps facts that are asked about after compression.
keywords:
  - kv cache compression
  - llm inference
  - long context
  - transformer
  - quantization
  - transform coding
  - pytorch
  - hugging face transformers
  - llama
